                    {
                        "sense_id": "86220580-47e3-3e32-9594-b726060a385f",
                        "entry_id": "e289304f-a7ad-3715-b571-e0f4a90a1130",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Elementarteilchen, das im Standardmodell der Teilchenphysik vorhergesagt und erstmals 2012 am CERN nachgewiesen wurde"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec388011-2009-4527-a41e-070274b8b70e",
                                "sense_id": "86220580-47e3-3e32-9594-b726060a385f",
                                "text": "Am Kernforschungszentrum CERN wird unter anderem versucht, die Existenz des Higgs-Bosons nachzuweisen."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e4941ae7-4c09-4467-a565-c8eed44e129c",
                        "source_entry_id": "e289304f-a7ad-3715-b571-e0f4a90a1130",
                        "source_sense_id": "86220580-47e3-3e32-9594-b726060a385f",
                        "target_lang_word": "希格斯玻色子",
                        "target_lang_code": "zh",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "希格斯玻色子",
                                "target_lang_code": "zh",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dabee97b-fcd2-3063-8c96-fd539472e262",
                                        "entry_id": "f5d3a307-18ea-33fa-8b99-50c16a3acc9c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "標準模型中的基本粒子，即自旋為零的玻色子，為其他粒子提供質量"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "84a31773-26ce-4765-9c7d-4c454c23755d",
                        "source_entry_id": "e289304f-a7ad-3715-b571-e0f4a90a1130",
                        "source_sense_id": "86220580-47e3-3e32-9594-b726060a385f",
                        "target_lang_word": "Higgs boson",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Higgs boson",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0614d1b9-4397-3344-886d-473aa56c5c05",
                                        "entry_id": "942c1ecc-3fad-3bcd-be78-971227d5f3b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An elementary particle in the Standard Model, namely a boson with zero spin, that gives mass to other particles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "particle"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b92569c-7618-4efb-9ef3-5992c54accd8",
                                                "sense_id": "0614d1b9-4397-3344-886d-473aa56c5c05",
                                                "text": "The existence of a Higgs boson would be the simplest solution to the problem of electroweak symmetry breaking."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7726bd5-6132-455b-9782-cae79182617a",
                                                "sense_id": "0614d1b9-4397-3344-886d-473aa56c5c05",
                                                "text": "We also know other things about the Higgs boson. If it were much more massive, a problem would occur. Since Higgs bosons interact with particles with a large mass, Higgs bosons would also interact with themselves (as they have mass too). This “self interaction” puts an upper limit on the mass of the Higgs boson as less than about 500-1000 GeV."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2255c939-643f-42d5-8db9-a7fe0c0f16f5",
                                                "sense_id": "0614d1b9-4397-3344-886d-473aa56c5c05",
                                                "text": "In the higher Higgs boson mass domain, the Higgs boson decays dominantly to a pair of b-quarks."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ce739ff-7a17-424d-987b-cdfb68d1dadb",
                                                "sense_id": "0614d1b9-4397-3344-886d-473aa56c5c05",
                                                "text": "Have you ever heard about the Higgs Boson Blues? / I'm going down to Geneva, baby / Gonna teach it to you"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "93b3c1f8-0dba-46a8-bd62-f5022650440b",
                        "source_entry_id": "e289304f-a7ad-3715-b571-e0f4a90a1130",
                        "source_sense_id": "86220580-47e3-3e32-9594-b726060a385f",
                        "target_lang_word": "boson de Higgs",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "boson de Higgs",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1756e762-410b-3a56-928d-dd651ced0398",
                                        "entry_id": "b4b71999-b409-3f0e-938c-7a4d7037d8a6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Particule élémentaire qui donne leur masse aux autres particules, notamment les bosons vecteurs de l’interaction électrofaible, dans le formalisme du modèle standard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c042bef-3534-4508-9293-472b4fa296ef",
                                                "sense_id": "1756e762-410b-3a56-928d-dd651ced0398",
                                                "text": "La recherche du boson de Higgs est une des priorités du LHC pour confirmer le modèle standard."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7d919a5-f5cf-4a59-84b8-0d84a1926047",
                                                "sense_id": "1756e762-410b-3a56-928d-dd651ced0398",
                                                "text": "Quelque chose ressemblant étrangement au boson de Higgs électrofaible a été découvert au Grand collisionneur de hadrons du CERN le 4 juillet 2012. C’est une particule neutre, de spin 0 et de masse s’élevant à 125 GeV."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "27fec6da-251d-47f7-a582-76d9ebc61840",
                        "source_entry_id": "e289304f-a7ad-3715-b571-e0f4a90a1130",
